  "verse": {
    "id": "v9",
    "lines": [
      {
        "words": [
          {
            "id": "w1",
            "text": "कालभैरवाष्टकं",
            "iast": "kālabhairavāṣṭakaṃ"
          },
          {
            "id": "w2",
            "text": "पठन्ति",
            "iast": "paṭhanti"
          },
          {
            "id": "w3",
            "text": "ये",
            "iast": "ye"
          },
          {
            "id": "w4",
            "text": "मनोहरं",
            "iast": "manoharaṃ"
          }
        ],
        "end": ""
      },
      {
        "words": [
          {
            "id": "w5",
            "text": "ज्ञानमुक्तिसाधनं",
            "iast": "jñānamuktisādhanaṃ"
          },
          {
            "id": "w6",
            "text": "विचित्रपुण्यवर्धनम्",
            "iast": "vicitrapuṇyavardhanam"
          }
        ],
        "end": "।"
      },
      {
        "words": [
          {
            "id": "w7",
            "text": "शोकमोहदैन्यलोभकोपतापनाशनं",
            "iast": "śokamohadainyalobhakopatāpanāśanaṃ"
          }
        ],
        "end": ""
      },
      {
        "words": [
          {
            "id": "w8",
            "text": "ते",
            "iast": "te"
          },
          {
            "id": "w9",
            "text": "प्रयान्ति",
            "iast": "prayānti"
          },
          {
            "id": "w10",
            "text": "कालभैरवाङ्घ्रिसन्निधिं",
            "iast": "kālabhairavāṅghrisannidhiṃ"
          },
          {
            "id": "w11",
            "text": "ध्रुवम्",
            "iast": "dhruvam"
          }
        ],
        "end": "॥ ९ ॥"
      }
    ],
    "annotations": [
      {
        "id": "a1",
        "refs": [
          "w9",
          "w10",
          "w11"
        ],
        "kind": "context",
        "body": {
          "en": "The hymn ends where it began. It opened at Kālabhairava's holy lotus feet (*pāvanāṅghri-paṅkaja*), [served by Indra, king of the gods](#v1-a1). The last line comes back to the same word, *aṅghri*, foot, and its closing claim puts the reciter there: *saṃnidhi*, nearness, presence. Those who recite the eight verses, the hymn says, surely (*dhruvam*) reach that nearness. The praise began at His feet and ends beside them.",
          "hi": "स्तोत्र वहीं समाप्त होता है जहाँ से आरम्भ हुआ था। यह कालभैरव के पावन चरण-कमलों (*पावनाङ्घ्रि-पङ्कज*) से खुला था, [जिनकी सेवा देवराज इन्द्र करते हैं](#v1-a1)। अन्तिम पंक्ति उसी शब्द *अङ्घ्रि*, चरण, पर लौटती है और अपने फल-कथन में पाठ करने वाले को वहीं रखती है: *सन्निधि*, यानी निकटता। स्तोत्र कहता है कि आठ श्लोकों का पाठ करने वाले निश्चय ही (*ध्रुवम्*) उस निकटता तक पहुँचते हैं। स्तुति चरणों से शुरू हुई थी और चरणों के पास ही पूरी होती है।"
        },
        "citations": [
          {
            "source": "vanivilas-1910-works-18",
            "locator": "transcriber's notes (verse 1 reading quoted)",
            "quote": "पावनाङ्घ्रिपङ्कज"
          },
          {
            "source": "mw-anghri",
