            "locator": "p. 204, verse 9, Hindi translation",
            "quote": "वे निश्चय ही कालभैरवके चरणोंकी संनिधि प्राप्त कर लेते हैं"
          },
          {
            "source": "mw-dhruvam",
            "locator": "MW dhruvam, p. 521",
            "quote": "certainly, surely"
          }
        ],
        "confidence": "medium"
      }
    ],
    "translations": {
      "en": {
        "lines": [
          [
            {
              "refs": [
                "w3"
              ],
              "text": "Those who"
            },
            {
              "refs": [
                "w2"
              ],
              "text": "recite"
            },
            {
              "refs": [
                "w4"
              ],
              "text": "the charming"
            },
            {
              "refs": [
                "w1"
              ],
              "text": "eight verses to Kālabhairava,"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "refs": [
                "w5"
              ],
              "text": "a means to knowledge and liberation,"
            },
            {
              "refs": [
                "w6"
              ],
              "text": "which makes wonderful merit grow"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "refs": [
                "w7"
              ],
              "text": "and destroys grief, delusion, misery, greed, anger and burning pain:"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "refs": [
                "w8"
              ],
              "text": "they"
            },
            {
              "refs": [
                "w11"
              ],
              "text": "surely"
            },
            {
              "refs": [
                "w9"
              ],
              "text": "reach"
            },
            {
              "refs": [
                "w10"
              ],
              "text": "the presence of Kālabhairava's feet."
            }
          ]
        ],
        "bhavartha": "The closing verse states what the hymn itself claims for those who recite it. These eight charming verses to Kālabhairava, it says, are a means to knowledge and liberation; they make merit grow and wipe away grief, delusion, misery, greed, anger and pain. Those who recite them, the verse declares, will surely come into the presence of Kālabhairava's feet, the feet where the hymn began."
      },
      "hi": {
        "lines": [
          [
            {
              "refs": [
                "w3"
              ],
              "text": "जो लोग"
            },
            {
              "refs": [
                "w4"
              ],
              "text": "मनोहर"
            },
            {
              "refs": [
                "w1"
              ],
              "text": "कालभैरवाष्टक का"
            },
            {
              "refs": [
                "w2"
              ],
              "text": "पाठ करते हैं,"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "refs": [
                "w5"
              ],
              "text": "जो ज्ञान और मुक्ति का साधन है,"
            },
            {
              "refs": [
                "w6"
              ],
              "text": "अद्भुत पुण्य को बढ़ाता है"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "refs": [
                "w7"
              ],
              "text": "और शोक, मोह, दीनता, लोभ, क्रोध तथा ताप का नाश करता है,"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "refs": [
                "w8"
              ],
              "text": "वे"
            },
            {
              "refs": [
                "w11"
              ],
              "text": "निश्चय ही"
            },
            {
              "refs": [
                "w10"
              ],
              "text": "कालभैरव के चरणों की सन्निधि में"
            },
            {
              "refs": [
                "w9"
              ],
              "text": "पहुँच जाते हैं।"
            }
          ]
        ],
        "bhavartha": "यह अन्तिम श्लोक बताता है कि स्तोत्र स्वयं अपने पाठ का क्या फल कहता है। इसके अनुसार कालभैरव के ये आठ मनोहर श्लोक ज्ञान और मुक्ति का साधन हैं, पुण्य को बढ़ाते हैं, और शोक, मोह, दीनता, लोभ, क्रोध तथा ताप को मिटाते हैं। श्लोक कहता है कि जो इनका पाठ करते हैं, वे निश्चय ही कालभैरव के चरणों की सन्निधि में पहुँच जाते हैं, उन्हीं चरणों तक जहाँ से स्तोत्र आरम्भ हुआ था।"
      }
    },
    "words": {
      "w1": {
        "compound": "c1",
        "padaccheda": [
          {
            "sa": "कालभैरव",
            "iast": "kālabhairava"
          },
          {
            "sa": "अष्टकम्",
            "iast": "aṣṭakam"
          }
        ],
        "sandhi": [
          {
            "name": "savarṇa-dīrgha",
            "rule": "a + a → ā",
            "explanation": {
              "en": "The final a of kālabhairava and the first a of aṣṭaka merge into one long ā: kālabhairava + aṣṭakam → kālabhairavāṣṭakam.",
              "hi": "कालभैरव का अन्तिम 'अ' और अष्टक का पहला 'अ' मिलकर एक दीर्घ 'आ' बन जाते हैं: कालभैरव + अष्टकम् → कालभैरवाष्टकम्।"
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "anusvāra",
            "rule": "m + consonant → ṃ",
